<title>USA: Disney's ABC names entertainment chairman.</title>
<headline>Disney's ABC names entertainment chairman.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co's ABC unit said Tuesday it named Stuart Bloomberg chairman of its entertainment division, succeeding Ted Harbert who resigned from the post earlier this year.</p>
<p>Bloomberg, who has 19 years programming experience at ABC, most recently served as president of ABC's Television Creative Development division.</p>
<p>In his new post, Bloomberg will oversee late night programming and the network's production ventures, ABC said in a statement.</p>
